<Base title="About this directory and our listing policy" description="How Hoarding Cleanup Finder compiles listings, what featured means, and how to correct or remove a listing.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About this directory</h1>
    <p>Hoarding Cleanup Finder is an independent directory of companies that do hoarding cleanup, biohazard and trauma cleanup, unattended death remediation and estate cleanouts in the United States. It exists because the people who need these services are usually dealing with a crisis and have no good way to find a vetted, local company.</p>
    <h2>Where listings come from</h2>
    <p>We compile listings from public business records and the companies' own websites. Before a listing goes live we check that the phone number and website are real. We write our own short descriptions and never copy text or photos from anywhere else. Listings are free and stay free.</p>
    <h2>What "verified", "owner-managed" and "featured" mean</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Verified</strong>: we confirmed the phone number and website and, where a state registration applies, checked it.</li>
      <li><strong>Owner-managed</strong>: the company has claimed the listing and maintains its own details.</li>
      <li><strong>Featured</strong>: the company pays a monthly fee for placement at the top of its city page. Featured listings are always labeled. Paying never affects whether a company is listed, and we do not accept payment to remove competitors.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Corrections and removals</h2>
    <p>If something on a listing is wrong, use the "report a correction" link on that page. If you run a company and want your listing removed, ask through the same link and we will remove it within one business day. We do not need a reason.</p>
    <h2>What we do with quote requests</h2>
    <p>When you send a request from a company page it goes to that company only. When you send one from a city or state page it goes to up to three companies near you, featured companies first. We keep the request so we can follow up if nobody responds. We do not sell your details to anyone else.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@hoardingcleanupfinder.com">hello@hoardingcleanupfinder.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
